+# Steel transfer instructions: a new Clearwater record, distinct objects and missing operative terms
+
+October 29, 2026. Existing B188/H005, AUD011/AUD016, SPT01–SPT08 and STL01–STL04 remain open. **One newly acquired official municipal source advances the transfer-record trail. It does not recover the artifact inventory or identify a disputed WTC 7 specimen.**
+
+The [December 13, 2010 Clearwater work-session minutes](https://clearwater.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?clip_id=1841&view_id=25#page=3), physical/printed pp. 3–4, item 3.2, identify artifact **G-0006**, citing a **January 31, 2007** inventory. They describe a 36-inch tube without visible identification marks and conditional cutting into two pieces. The item seeks authorization to sign/accept; it does not by itself prove adoption, execution, shipment, cutting or receipt. Page 4 also uses **“holds neither”** in describing indemnification. Preserve the wording; its own operative agreement is needed before assigning legal effect. CW01–CW03 in [COMPARISON.json](COMPARISON.json).
+
+The [earlier Beverly Hills packet](https://beverlyhills.granicus.com/MetaViewer.php?clip_id=2444&meta_id=136233&view_id=11#page=2) concerns a different artifact, visually read **I-0137** (raw extraction **1-0137**). Staff reports nonalteration on p. 2. Its reproduced order, pp. 11–12, reserves inspection/testing for litigation parties or their representatives upon ten days notice. The [preceding review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/240914e0f1851956e74dae61a076e6cd52c45847/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-artifact-transfer-orders-2026-10-27/README.md) found no equivalent express nonalteration clause in the attached letter/order; any separate instruction remains unacquired. These accounts and source layers are retained unchanged. This unit newly re-viewed p. 2 and pp. 11–12; the remainder relies on the earlier qualified review.
+
+## What the comparison actually tests
+
+Different recipient/object instructions do not establish a contradiction about the same transaction. Neither record proves a uniform preservation rule. A hypothetical blanket claim that every distributed artifact had an identical nonalteration condition would need to account for Clearwater's contrary description. Conversely, a staff summary cannot certify the terms or implementation of its missing signed agreement. The strongest competing reading is item-specific permission or differing document scope; that remains an untested explanation, not a resolution.
+
+The shared January 2007 inventory reference provides a concrete retrieval key, not a complete custody chain. The October 2004 completion account ([2005 minutes, p. 6](https://dspace.njstatelib.org/server/api/core/bitstreams/c960df66-1aba-40cd-9eb0-140585e3be89/content#page=6)), 2006 completion account ([2012 LMDC report, p. 5](https://www.renewnyc.org/attachments/content/pdfs/WTC_Historic_Resources_Report_January_2012.pdf#page=5)) and January 31, 2007 reference remain side by side. Those two earlier accounts are inherited from the [preserved study](../steel-preservation-decisions-2026-10-27/README.md), not newly source-read here. We have not obtained the editions, change history, item crosswalks or delivery records. No arithmetic on unlike collections, inferred alias match, authenticity finding, deliberate destruction or concealment inference is supported here. A physically unmarked item can have an administrative inventory number; that combination alone is not inconsistent.
+
+The decisive tests remain obtaining each signed agreement and incorporated order/instruction, the referenced inventory entry/photo and revisions, and actual dispatch/receipt/cutting/condition logs. Compare permission, performance and later condition separately. Neither object has been joined to W14A/B, C12a/b, FEMA Sample 1 or a NIST-retained coupon. The inspection condition in the held Beverly Hills order is meaningful contrary evidence to a blanket loss-of-testing-rights claim; it is not proof of an experiment or a right applying to the public or to Clearwater's item.
+
+## Acquisition, reading and reproducibility
+
+CW2010 is a newly acquired 26-page, 141,452-byte municipal PDF; SHA-256 `c0202fb6da7681f4d064bc091ab9834420874118926beed26bf9d994f29aa179`. Two selected page images were read. BH2011 is the unchanged 12-page municipal copy; SHA-256 `140f527241183d46aba69b89533e115ef7a06d15b7a3c17f7d0a7355066a0b3a`; three selected page images were re-read. No video was reviewed, no OCR was run, signatures were not authenticated, and the actual inventory and Clearwater agreement remain missing. [SOURCES.json](SOURCES.json) and [COMPARISON.json](COMPARISON.json) supply URLs, access times, roles and physical/page-local extraction locators. Text extraction is a derivative; matching a text anchor does not authenticate historical assertions.
+
+Eight new indexed queries reached the frozen cap; one malformed domain query was ineffective and is logged locally. The exact public agenda link exposed by the player failed DNS resolution; the steel-item annotation returned navigation script rather than an agreement. Do not treat either access outcome as evidence of historical removal. An existing journal inventory-caption route supplied no newly acquired inventory; a previously failed image was not retried. Full acquisition/parser/error receipts remain local. Two parser/runtime setup errors were corrected without changing any source bytes.
+
+`verify_records.py --clearwater-pdf PATH --beverly-pdf PATH` verifies both entity hashes/page counts, selected literal anchors and the shared date/different-ID reference test. It does not test actual custody, authority, specimen identity or historical truth. [RESULTS.json](RESULTS.json) is the executed documentary result; [OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) preserves the unperformed tests and all five track dependencies. [REVIEW-AND-CHECKS.json](REVIEW-AND-CHECKS.json) gives actual scope/checklist and predecessor status. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) records only these additive notes. Earlier sources, reports and conflicting values are untouched.
+
+Only reviewed research notes, safe locators and verification artifacts enter this public addition. Raw sources/renders, signatures/contact data, private correspondence, internal coordination and strategy remain outside its payload. No outreach, fees, request or filing, physical sampling, deletion, private push, merge or history rewrite occurred. Documentary acquisition/testing and any verified publication are partial milestones; the substantive five-track goal remains open.
